========================================
            Tmux Cheatsheet
========================================

--- Starting & Managing Sessions ---

- Start a new session:
  tmux
  or with a custom name:
  tmux new -s mysession

- List sessions:
  tmux ls

- Attach to a session:
  tmux attach -t mysession

- Kill a session:
  tmux kill-session -t mysession

----------------------------------------

--- Prefix Key ---

- Default Prefix: Ctrl+b
  (This key combination must be pressed before most tmux commands.)

- Change Prefix (in ~/.tmux.conf):
  set -g prefix C-a
  unbind C-b
  bind C-a send-prefix

----------------------------------------

--- Session Management Commands ---

- Detach from a session:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then d)

----------------------------------------

--- Window Management ---

- Create a new window:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then c)

- List windows:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then w)

- Rename current window:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then ,)

- Switch to next window:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then n)

- Switch to previous window:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then p)

- Select window by number:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then <number>)

- Kill current window:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then &)

----------------------------------------

--- Pane Management ---

- Split window vertically (side-by-side):
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then %)

- Split window horizontally (top/bottom):
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then ")

- Switch between panes:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then arrow keys or o to cycle through)

- Resize pane:
  Enter command mode with (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then :)
  and type one of the following:
    resize-pane -L 10   # Resize 10 cells to the left
    resize-pane -R 10   # Resize 10 cells to the right
    resize-pane -U 10   # Resize 10 cells upward
    resize-pane -D 10   # Resize 10 cells downward
  (You can also bind these commands to keys in your ~/.tmux.conf.)

- Swap panes:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then { or })

- Kill current pane:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then x)

- Zoom (toggle fullscreen) current pane:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then z)

----------------------------------------

--- Copy Mode (Scrollback) ---

- Enter copy mode:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then [)

- Navigate in copy mode:
  Use arrow keys or Page Up/Page Down.
  If using vi-like bindings, you can also use h, j, k, l.

- Exit copy mode:
  Press q or Esc

- Copy text (using vi bindings):
  1. Press Space to start selection.
  2. Move the cursor to select text.
  3. Press Enter to copy the selection.

----------------------------------------

--- Command Prompt ---

- Access tmux command prompt:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then :)

- Reload tmux configuration:
  In the command prompt, type:
    source-file ~/.tmux.conf

- List all key bindings:
  (Press Prefix: Ctrl+b then ?)

----------------------------------------

--- Mouse Mode ---

- Enable mouse support (add to ~/.tmux.conf):
  set -g mouse on
  (This allows clicking to select panes, resize, and switch windows.)

----------------------------------------

--- Custom Key Bindings Example ---

To add quick pane resizing shortcuts, add the following lines to your ~/.tmux.conf:

  bind -r H resize-pane -L 5
  bind -r J resize-pane -D 5
  bind -r K resize-pane -U 5
  bind -r L resize-pane -R 5

This lets you use "Prefix + H/J/K/L" to resize the active pane by 5 cells in the corresponding direction.

========================================
Happy Multiplexing with tmux!
========================================

